                        Narrate(text: "Given enough water, the whole crystal comes apart like this: the salt dissolves. The ions are not destroyed. They spread through the water as separate Na⁺ and Cl⁻ ions, each surrounded by water molecules. This is a salt solution. If the water evaporates, the ions join up again into crystals.", for_s: 12.0),
                        Highlight(part: "na-330"),
                        Highlight(part: "cl-333"),
                        Highlight(part: "na-033"),
                        Highlight(part: "cl-030"),
                    ]),
                ]),
            ]),
    ],
)
